SentimentEngagementAnalyzer
===========================
A modular Python framework for predicting Tesla daily stock returns by
combining FinBERT-derived social media sentiment features with OHLCV-based
technical indicators.

Architecture
------------
  TweetPreprocessor            — raw tweet cleaning and optional FinBERT inference
  SentimentFeatureEngineer     — daily sentiment feature construction
  TechnicalFeatureEngineer     — OHLCV technical indicator construction
  StatisticalValidator         — LINE-style diagnostics, nested tests, bootstrap CI
  SentimentEngagementAnalyzer  — unified fit/predict/summary/plot API
  RealTimeInferenceEngine      — optional yfinance-based inference utilities

Statistical Tests Implemented
-----------------------------
  - Nested F-test (baseline vs sentiment-enhanced)
  - Bootstrap ΔR² confidence intervals (default 1,000 iterations)
  - Durbin-Watson autocorrelation test
  - Ljung-Box Q-test for residual independence
  - Shapiro-Wilk normality test
  - Jarque-Bera normality test
  - Breusch-Pagan homoscedasticity test
  - Variance Inflation Factor (VIF) multicollinearity analysis
  - OLS coefficient t-tests with confidence intervals (for inference summaries)
  - AIC, BIC, adjusted R²
  - No-information benchmarks (random walk, mean predictor)

Prediction Intervals
--------------------
  - Conformal (default after training): uses the (1-α) quantile of |train residuals|
    to produce finite-sample, distribution-free intervals: ŷ ± q̂
  - Fallback: t-based interval using training residual std (if conformal not available)

Visualizations Produced
-----------------------
  - Baseline vs full model comparison bar charts (R², RMSE, MAE)
  - Time-series of actual vs predicted returns with prediction intervals
  - Actual vs predicted scatter plot
  - Residuals vs predicted plot
  - Normal Q-Q plot
  - Residual distribution histogram
  - Feature importance bar chart with confidence intervals (colour-coded by p-value)
  - Feature correlation heatmap

Usage
-----
  from sentiment_engagement_analyzer import (
      SentimentEngagementAnalyzer, ModelConfig, ModelType,
      TweetPreprocessor, RealTimeInferenceEngine
  )

  config   = ModelConfig(model_type=ModelType.RIDGE, verbose=True)
  analyzer = SentimentEngagementAnalyzer(config)
  analyzer.fit(stock_df, tweet_df)
  analyzer.summary()
  analyzer.plot("all")

